Chapter 6: Operational Independence with Parametric β

6.1 The Two Channels

Definition 6.1 (Verification channels). Channel 1 (M2) generates hypotheses via an LLM, scored by Z_1. Channel 2 (M3) searches for counterexamples via digital-twin physics residuals, scored by Z_2.

Definition 6.2 (Common-cause factor). \beta \in (0,1) is the fraction of total failure probability attributable to shared causes.

6.2 Parametric Shared-Error Bound

Proposition 6.1 (Parametric bound). Under the \beta-factor model,

P(\text{both err} \mid s) \le (1 - \beta)^2 p_e^2 + \beta p_e

Proof. As in Proposition 2.2. \square

Remark 6.1. The \beta-factor model is standard in common-cause failure analysis. Typical conservative values are \beta \in [0.05, 0.10]. The theorems of HARC are parametric in \beta: they hold for any \beta \in (0,1), and the bound tightens as \beta \to 0.

Remark 6.2. The "by design" axiom is eliminated. The \beta parameter is measurable or conservatively bounded.

