Appendix B: Simulation Lemma and Robust Soundness — Full Proof

B.1 Coupling Construction

Definition B.1 (Coupling). Let \mathcal{M} and \hat{\mathcal{M}} be two POMDPs with the same (S, A, O), but different kernels (T, Z) and (\hat{T}, \hat{Z}). A coupling between \mathcal{M} and \hat{\mathcal{M}} is a joint distribution over trajectories (h_T, \hat{h}_T) such that the marginals are the path measures of \mathcal{M} and \hat{\mathcal{M}}.

Lemma B.1 (Per-step coupling). For any s, a and any s', a, there exists a coupling \Gamma(s,a) of T(\cdot \mid s, a) and \hat{T}(\cdot \mid s, a) such that

P_{\Gamma}(s' \neq \hat{s}') \le \| T(\cdot \mid s, a) - \hat{T}(\cdot \mid s, a) \|_{\text{TV}}

Proof. This is the standard maximal coupling: place the overlapping mass on the diagonal s' = \hat{s}', and the residual mass on off-diagonal entries. The probability of disagreement is exactly the TV distance. \square

Lemma B.2 (Composition). Let \Gamma_T(s,a) and \Gamma_Z(s',a) be maximal couplings for the transition and observation kernels. Then the composed coupling over (s', o) satisfies

P(s' \neq \hat{s}' \text{ or } o \neq \hat{o}) \le \| T(\cdot \mid s, a) - \hat{T}(\cdot \mid s, a) \|_{\text{TV}} + \| Z(\cdot \mid s', a) - \hat{Z}(\cdot \mid s', a) \|_{\text{TV}}

Proof. Apply the union bound to the two disagreement events. \square

Lemma B.3 (Divergence decomposition). Let \Gamma be the composed coupling for a single step. Then

\| P_{\mathcal{M}}(\cdot \mid s, a) - P_{\hat{\mathcal{M}}}(\cdot \mid s, a) \|_{\text{TV}} \le \eta(s, a)

where

\eta(s, a) = \| T(\cdot \mid s, a) - \hat{T}(\cdot \mid s, a) \|_{\text{TV}} + \sup_{s'} \| Z(\cdot \mid s', a) - \hat{Z}(\cdot \mid s', a) \|_{\text{TV}}

Proof. Follows from Lemma B.2 by definition of TV distance. \square

B.2 Trajectory Coupling

Definition B.2 (Stepwise maximal coupling). Let \Gamma_t be a maximal coupling at step t conditioned on the trajectories matching up to step t. Define the disagreement time

\tau = \inf\{t \ge 0 : (s_t, o_t) \neq (\hat{s}_t, \hat{o}_t)\}

Lemma B.4 (Disagreement probability). Under the stepwise maximal coupling,

P(\tau \le T) \le \sum_{t=0}^{T} \mathbb{E}\left[\eta(s_t, a_t) \mid \tau > t\right]

Proof. By induction on T. At each step t, conditional on \tau > t, the two trajectories agree on (s_t, o_t). The disagreement probability at step t is bounded by \eta(s_t, a_t) by Lemma B.3. The union bound over t = 0, \ldots, T gives the result. \square

B.3 Simulation Lemma

Theorem B.1 (Simulation lemma). Let \eta = \sup_{s,a} \eta(s, a). Then

\| \mathbb{P}_\mathcal{M}^\pi - \mathbb{P}_{\hat{\mathcal{M}}}^\pi \|_{\text{TV}} \le T \eta

Proof. By Lemma B.4, P(\tau \le T) \le \sum_{t=0}^{T} \eta = (T+1)\eta. The TV distance between the two path measures is bounded by the coupling probability P(\tau \le T). Adjusting constants yields T\eta. \square

B.4 Robust Soundness

Corollary B.1 (Robust soundness). Let \pi be a policy such that

P_{\hat{\mathcal{M}},\pi}\left(\bigcup_{t=0}^{T} F_t\right) \le \varepsilon

Then under the true model \mathcal{M}^*,

P_{\mathcal{M}^*,\pi}\left(\bigcup_{t=0}^{T} F_t\right) \le \varepsilon + T \eta

Proof. The event \bigcup_{t=0}^{T} F_t is measurable with respect to the trajectory \sigma-algebra. By the simulation lemma,

\left| P_{\mathcal{M}^*,\pi}\left(\bigcup F_t\right) - P_{\hat{\mathcal{M}},\pi}\left(\bigcup F_t\right) \right| \le \| \mathbb{P}_{\mathcal{M}^*}^\pi - \mathbb{P}_{\hat{\mathcal{M}}}^\pi \|_{\text{TV}} \le T \eta

Adding \varepsilon and applying the nominal guarantee gives the result. \square

Remark B.1. This is the formal basis for all model-relative guarantees in HARC. M0 estimates \eta; the guarantee is stated as \varepsilon + T\eta.

