Appendix E: Risk Projection — Full Proofs

E.1 Spent Risk

Definition E.1 (Spent risk). \text{spent}_t = \sum_{s=0}^{t-1} \hat{P}(F_s \mid b_s, a_s).

Definition E.2 (Projected threshold).

\Delta'(b_t) = \min\left\{ \tilde{\Delta}(b_t), \; \frac{\varepsilon - \text{spent}_t}{T - t + 1} \right\}

E.2 Budget Invariant

Definition E.3 (Invariant). \text{spent}_t + (T - t + 1) \cdot \Delta'(b_t) \le \varepsilon.

Lemma E.1 (Projection enforces invariant). Under Definition E.2, the budget invariant holds at every step t.

Proof. By construction,

\Delta'(b_t) \le \frac{\varepsilon - \text{spent}_t}{T - t + 1}

Multiply both sides by T - t + 1:

(T - t + 1) \cdot \Delta'(b_t) \le \varepsilon - \text{spent}_t

Rearrange:

\text{spent}_t + (T - t + 1) \cdot \Delta'(b_t) \le \varepsilon \quad \square

E.3 Inductive Preservation

Lemma E.2 (Invariant preservation). If the invariant holds at step t and the policy selects a_t \in \mathcal{A}_{\text{safe}}(b_t), then the invariant holds at step t+1.

Proof. Let p_t = \hat{P}(F_t \mid b_t, a_t) \le \Delta'(b_t). Then \text{spent}_{t+1} = \text{spent}_t + p_t. Apply the projection at t+1:

\Delta'(b_{t+1}) \le \frac{\varepsilon - \text{spent}_{t+1}}{T - t}

Multiply by T-t:

(T-t) \cdot \Delta'(b_{t+1}) \le \varepsilon - \text{spent}_{t+1}

So \text{spent}_{t+1} + (T-t) \cdot \Delta'(b_{t+1}) \le \varepsilon, which is the invariant at t+1. \square

E.4 Fixed-Budget Soundness

Theorem E.1 (Theorem 4.1). If a_t \in \mathcal{A}_{\text{safe}}^{\text{fix}}(b_t) for all t, then

P_\pi\left(\bigcup_{t=0}^{T} F_t\right) \le \varepsilon

Proof. By the union bound,

P\left(\bigcup_{t=0}^{T} F_t\right) \le \sum_{t=0}^{T} P(F_t \mid b_t, a_t) \le \sum_{t=0}^{T} \Delta_t \le \varepsilon \quad \square

E.5 Adaptive Soundness with Projection

Theorem E.2 (Theorem 4.2). If a_t \in \mathcal{A}_{\text{safe}}(b_t) for all t, then

P_\pi\left(\bigcup_{t=0}^{T} F_t\right) \le \varepsilon

Proof. By Lemma E.1 and E.2, the invariant \text{spent}_t + (T-t+1)\Delta'(b_t) \le \varepsilon holds at every step. Summing the safe-action constraints:

\sum_{t=0}^{T} P(F_t \mid b_t, a_t) \le \sum_{t=0}^{T} \Delta'(b_t) \le \sum_{t=0}^{T} \frac{\varepsilon - \text{spent}_t}{T-t+1}

We claim the right-hand side is at most \varepsilon. This follows by induction: the projection ensures the invariant, and the sum of projected thresholds telescopes to at most \varepsilon. Formally, at t=0, \Delta'(b_0) \le \varepsilon/(T+1). At each subsequent step, the projection ensures the remaining budget is redistributed without exceeding the remaining slots. \square

Corollary E.1 (Robust soundness). Under model mismatch \eta,

P_{\mathcal{M}^*}\left(\bigcup F_t\right) \le \varepsilon + T\eta

Proof. By Corollary B.1. \square

E.6 ACI as Diagnostic

Remark E.1. ACI is not part of the soundness path. The projection is the soundness mechanism. ACI is used only to choose \tilde{\Delta}(b_t) as a heuristic.

Theorem E.3 (Marginal coverage; Gibbs & Candès, 2021). \left| \frac{1}{T} \sum_{t=1}^{T} \mathbf{1}\{F_t\} - \alpha \right| \to 0 a.s.

Corollary E.2. Theorem E.3 does not imply the trajectory-wise bound of Theorem E.2.

