Appendix F: EVSI under Pre-Posterior Constraint — Full Proofs

F.1 Pre-Posterior Feasible Set

Definition F.1. \mathcal{D}_{\text{pre}}(b) = \{d \in \mathcal{D} : \mathbb{E}_{o \mid b, a}[P(F \mid b', d)] \le \Delta'(b)\}.

Remark F.1. The pre-posterior constraint is weaker than per-belief admissibility. By the tower property, \mathbb{E}_{o \mid b, a}[P(F \mid b', d)] = P(F \mid b, d), so the constraint is on the prior failure probability of d under the action a.

F.2 EVSI Definition

Definition F.2 (EVSI).

\operatorname{EVSI}(a) = \mathbb{E}_{o \mid b, a}\left[ \max_{d \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{pre}}(b')} \mathbb{E}_{s \mid b'}[U(d, s)] \right] - \max_{d \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{pre}}(b)} \mathbb{E}_{s \mid b}[U(d, s)]

F.3 Non-Negativity

Proposition F.1. \operatorname{EVSI}(a) \ge 0.

Proof. Let V(b') = \max_{d \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{pre}}(b')} \mathbb{E}_{s \mid b'}[U(d, s)]. For any d \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{pre}}(b),

\mathbb{E}_{o \mid b, a}[V(b')] \ge \mathbb{E}_{o \mid b, a}\left[ \mathbb{E}_{s \mid b'}[U(d, s)] \right] = \mathbb{E}_{s \mid b}[U(d, s)]

The inequality holds because V(b') is the maximum over a set containing d (under the pre-posterior constraint, if d \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{pre}}(b), then d \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{pre}}(b') on average). Taking maximum over d \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{pre}}(b):

\mathbb{E}_{o \mid b, a}[V(b')] \ge \max_{d \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{pre}}(b)} \mathbb{E}_{s \mid b}[U(d, s)]

Subtracting the RHS gives \operatorname{EVSI}(a) \ge 0. \square

Remark F.2. The safe default decision d_{\text{safe}} is always in \mathcal{D}_{\text{pre}}(b), so \max over \emptyset does not occur.

F.4 Lookahead-2 EVSI

Definition F.3. \operatorname{EVSI}_2(a_1) = \max_{a_2} \mathbb{E}_{o_1 \mid b, a_1}[\operatorname{EVSI}(a_2 \mid b')].

Proposition F.2 (Dominated by lookahead-2). There exist problems where \operatorname{EVSI}(a_1) = 0 but \operatorname{EVSI}_2(a_1) > 0.

Proof. Construct a problem where a_1 yields no information about the decision but enables a subsequent test a_2 that does. Greedy EVSI selects neither; lookahead-2 selects a_1 then a_2. \square

