Appendix K: Monte Carlo Validation — Full Protocol

K.1 Synthetic Human

Definition K.1. A synthetic human is a stochastic policy \pi_H^{\text{syn}} with known categorical parameter \boldsymbol{\mu}^* and known delay d^*.

K.2 Validation of Theorem 4.1

Procedure K.1.

1. Initialize b_0, \mathcal{E}_0 = \emptyset.
2. For each episode k = 1, \ldots, K:
   a. Sample h^* \sim b_0.
   b. For t = 0, \ldots, T:
   · Sample a^H_t \sim \pi_H^{\text{syn}}(\cdot \mid z_t, a^R_t).
   · Execute a^{\text{exec}}_t = \text{pop}(q_t).
   · Sample F_t \sim \text{Bernoulli}(P(F \mid b_t, a_t)).
   · If F_t = 1, record failure.
   · Update belief b_{t+1}.
   · Select a^R_{t+1} \in \mathcal{A}_{\text{safe}}(b_{t+1}).
3. Estimate \hat{P}(\bigcup F_t) = \frac{1}{K} \sum_k \mathbf{1}\{\text{failure in episode } k\}.

