Appendix L: Architecture — Full Module Specifications

L.1 M0 — Model-Adequacy Gate

Input: belief b, model \mathcal{M}, observed data s^{\text{obs}}.
Output: {adequate, inadequate}.
Contract: If inadequate, output undemonstrated.
Formal: \text{M0}(b) = \text{inadequate} if p_{\text{PPP}} < \gamma_{\text{low}} or p_{\text{PPP}} > \gamma_{\text{high}}.
Role in robust soundness: M0 estimates \eta. The robust bound is \varepsilon + T\eta.

L.2 M1 — Context Anchor

Input: user facts \mathcal{F}, AI hypotheses \mathcal{H}_{\text{AI}}.
Output: typed context graph \mathcal{G} = (V, E) with node types {FACT, HYPOTHESIS, INFERENCE} and provenance edges.
Contract: Every node is typed; every HYPOTHESIS is traceable to a FACT or an AI proposal.

L.3 M2 — Hypothesis Explorer

Input: context graph \mathcal{G}, history h_t.
Output: hypothesis set \{h_i\}_{i=1}^{N} with calibrated priors, plus h_{\text{catch-all}} with diffuse likelihood.
Surprise trigger: \max_i P(h_i \mid b) < \delta_{\text{surprise}} or \prod_i Z(o \mid h_i, a) < \delta_{\text{likelihood}}.

L.4 M3 — Adversarial Examiner

Input: hypothesis set, history.
Output: counterexamples, contradictions, missing-data list.
Contract: M3 uses Z_2 with shared-cause factor \beta relative to M2's Z_1.

L.5 M4 — Test Selector

Input: belief b, safe action set \mathcal{A}_{\text{safe}}(b).
Output: a_{\text{test}}^* = \arg\max_{a \in \mathcal{A}_{\text{safe}}(b)} \operatorname{EVSI}_2(a).
Contract: EVSI computed under pre-posterior constraint. Tests with P(F^{\text{test-induced}} \mid b, a) > \Delta'(b) are excluded.

L.6 M5 — Safety Gate

Level Condition Authority Human Model
1 Pre-certified, P(F) < \varepsilon_{\text{auto}} Automatic —
2 Calibrated evidence, moderate risk Human confirmation \rho_h, \tau_h modeled
3 Partial evidence, high risk Committee \delta_{\text{takeover}} modeled
4 Insufficient evidence or P(F) > \varepsilon Prohibition —

L.7 M6 — Evidence Memory

Schema:

\text{Evidence} = \{\text{test\_id}, \text{observation}, \text{timestamp}, \text{sensor\_id}, \text{hash}, \text{prover}\}

Accept predicate:

\text{Accept}(b_T, \mathcal{E}_T) = 1 \iff \begin{cases}
\text{mandatory\_tests} \subseteq \mathcal{E}_T.\text{tests} \\
\wedge \text{invariants\_checked} \\
\wedge \text{auth\_sig\_valid} \\
\wedge \text{Brier} < \theta_{\text{Brier}} \\
